title: "pallet-delegated-staking: reject zero-amount delegations for new delegators"
doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      A zero-amount delegation for a new delegator no longer stores an empty Delegation
      record or takes a provider reference. Before, it left the account marked as a
      delegator, which blocked it from registering as an agent.

      do_delegate and migrate_delegation reject a zero amount for a new delegator, and
      Delegation::update stores nothing for a new zero-amount entry. A zero top-up on an
      existing delegation is unchanged (still a no-op), which nomination-pools relies on for
      bond_extra at 100% commission.
crates:
  - name: pallet-delegated-staking
    bump: patch
